<text>

The code statements that lead to the bug are:
data = devm_kzalloc(&intf->dev, sizeof(*data), GFP_KERNEL);
Reason:
`devm_kzalloc` ties the lifetime of the `btusb_data` structure to the first USB interface (`&intf->dev`). When `btusb_disconnect()` calls `usb_driver_release_interface()` on that interface (e.g., `usb_driver_release_interface(&btusb_driver, data->intf)`), the devm framework automatically frees `data` while other interfaces (ISOC, DIAG) still reference it, causing a use-after-free.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
data = kzalloc(sizeof(*data), GFP_KERNEL);
...
